{"availability":"available","full":"scriptex/at-the-wall","name":"at-the-wall","description":"A Game of Thrones scene coded in pure SCSS and HTML","category":"Design","language":"HTML","stars":16,"forks":4,"created":"2018-09-01T04:56:07Z","updated":"2026-10-11T05:28:02Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://at-the-wall.atanas.info","topics":["drawing","game-of-thrones","pure-css","scene"],"demo":"https://codepen.io/scriptex/full/eLWdKN/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T07:10:09.875Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T07:10:09.875Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T07:10:09.875Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.625Z","stars":16,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-17T07:10:09.875Z","stars":16,"forks":4}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A scene from Game of Thrones coded in CSS and HTML. There are no images used whatsoever - only code.","This is the combined work of several frontend developers, including me. The purpose was to learn new things and work in a larger team. As a result we achieved a complex and animations-heavy interactive drawing using SCSS and HTML only.","The team was split into smaller teams (two devs) and each team worked on a part of the drawing. For example: Jon Snow, The White Walker, the sky, the snowflakes, the wall, the ground and the trees. I coded the White Walker and supervised the team, provided solutions or hints where needed and when everyone was done I merged their work in a single repository."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/scriptex/at-the-wall/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"65b146c52ee761a25e310700c991c5fcb3079f2c607e961e98fbadc59c70b536","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.675Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.675Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A scene from Game of Thrones coded in CSS and HTML. There are no images used whatsoever - only code.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/scriptex/at-the-wall/blob/maste